{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/promethean-the-created-aa/1497325-revised-cannibalize-a-homebrew-reworking","id":1497325,"title":"Revised Cannibalize -- a homebrew reworking.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Promethean: The Created"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-16T16:28:53-08:00","id":1497325,"title":"Revised Cannibalize -- a homebrew reworking.","content":"The Cannibalize Alembic, one of the Flux Transmutations added in <b>Night Horrors: The Tormented</b>, is completely borked. It follows none of the rules for how Transumations are supposed to work:<ul><li>Alembics are supposed to be &quot;Charged&quot; with Pyros, activating the ability to use a particular Distillation for a scene. If there are further Pyros expenditures (such as with Arc), those are usually specifically called out. Cannibalize, OTOH, seems to assume Pyros expenditure on a per-use basis.</li> <li>The Pyros costs for the abilities gained are grossly disproportional to the benefits gained, especially when compared to something like Transhuman Potential. Not only do you have to pay numerous Pyros for the abilities but you have to eat abilities that are already greater than your own to gain any benefit from skill or attributes. Angel, the Centimanus in the book that has this power as her signature ability, already has decently high (3+ dots) in almost all of her Attributes, and most of the Skills she'd want to buff (given her write-up) she already has. This creates a Nonbo situation -- she'd need to spend a lot of Pyros to buff abilities she's never going to use with the frequency such an expenditure would justify.</li> <li>There is no guidance for <i>when</i> Cannibalize can be used. Can it be used while the creature is still living? Or does she have to kill them first? The only Distillation that even discusses damage is the last one, but eating someone's Encyclopedic Knowledge or Weaponry skill would presumably inflict damage as well.</li> <li>The durations are measured in regular time unites (hours and days) rather than in-game units (Scenes, Chapters, Stories).</li> <li>The Persistent Ability mentions a &quot;an additional die of damage with all bite attacks.&quot; This is not how weapon ratings work in CoD 2e, where damage isn't rated in Dice, but in Levels.</li> </ul>Given these issues, I've attempted to rework the Alembic completely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-size:20px\"><b>Cannibalize</b></span><br /> <br /> The power of Flux is limitless, eternal, and vast as the sky itself, yet hidden within the confines of a crack in the ceiling only the Centimani have the clarity to find. It is this contradiction in Flux that leads many Freaks to eventually abandon it, yet the true Centimanus who sees through the crack and beyond the lie knows those errant fools were simply not ready to see Flux for what it truly is. The devout Freak spends years preparing their mind and body for the rigors of true enlightenment. Flux also provides, however, for those that don\u2019t have that sort of time. With a bit of due diligence and a suppressed gag reflex, a Freak can consume the strengths of others to prepare themselves for the trials to come. Mortal and supernal creatures alike all become a feast for the ravenous Freak.<br /> <br /> <b>Persistent</b>: The jaws of the Centimanus are incredibly strong. They can make bite attacks that deal lethal damage, without needing to grapple a foe first. If another power already gives them the capacity for lethal blows, add one to their unarmed weapon modifier instead.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Aptitude</b></span><br /> <br /> With this level of the Alembic charged, The Freak may consume the physical and mental Merits of other beings with a successful bite attack. This cannibalism must make sense in context of the Merit being consumed \u2014 for example, the Freak might eat the body of a large man to gain Huge Size, or the brain of a professor to gain Encyclopedic Knowledge. This ability can steal Style Merits, if applicable. This may require a Called Shot at the Storyteller's discretion. The Centimanus can even eat the corpses of the dead to gain the abilities, as long as the body's fresh (typically died within the same Chapter).<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 1 Pyros<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Resolve + Stamina + Azoth - Merit Rating (Reflexive), or Resolve + Stamina + Azoth (Instant)<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive after a successful Bite attack, or Instant if eating an already dead creature.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Roll Results</b></span><ul><li><b>Success</b>: The Centimanus gains the relevant Merit at the victim's dot rating for the rest of the chapter. If the Centimanus already possesses the Merit, they instead gain one dot in the Merit's rating (up to the Merit's maximum).</li> <li><b>Exceptional Success</b>: The Freak an exceptional affinity with the new configuration of their body, allowing her to retain the consumed Merit longer. The consumed merit lasts for the rest of the Story.</li> <li><b>Failure</b>: The Freak gains nothing.</li> <li><b>Dramatic Failure</b>: Something gets twisted while the Freak transmutes the new element into their being, inflicting them with a Condition or Tilt related to the Merit they were trying to consume. For example, a Freak trying to steal Fleet of Foot might become Crippled, or one attempting to gain Danger Sense might instead become Frightened.</li> </ul><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Acumen</b></span><br /> <br /> With this level of the Alembic charged, The Freak may consume the Skills of another being with a successful Bite attack. They consume body parts in some way related to the ability: eyeballs for Investigation or a hand for Weaponry, which may require a Called Shot at the Storyteller's discretion. The Centimanus can even eat the corpses of the dead to gain the abilities, as long as the body's fresh (typically died within the same Chapter).<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 2 Pyros<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Resolve + Stamina + Azoth - Skill Rating (Reflexive), or Resolve + Stamina + Azoth (Instant)<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive, after a successful Bite attack, or Instant, if eating an already dead creature.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Roll Results</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Success</b>: The Freak can internalize the Skill. They gain one dot in the Skill in question, up to their Trait Maximum, for the rest of the scene. If the victim\u2019s rating in the Skill is equal to or higher than the Freak\u2019s, they gain two dots. The duration can be increased to 24 hours by spending an additional point of Pyros, and can be extended by spending another Pyros every day, to a maximum of (Azoth) days.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: The Centimanus gleans exceptional insight, gaining two additional dots in the Skill instead of one (or thee instead of two), even if this takes them above their trait maximum. This bonus lasts the rest of the scene; any dots above the Freak's Trait maximum fade, but the remainder last until the end of the chapter.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: The flesh is consumed but the knowledge escapes.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: Something goes horribly awry in the mystic furnace that is the Freak\u2019s gut. For the remainder of the scene, they are afflicted with the Sick (grave) Tilt.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Endowment</b></span><br /> <br /> With this level of the Alembic charged, The Freak may consume the Attributes of another being with a successful Bite attack. The parts should be related in some way to Attribute they are ingesting (tendon or ligaments for Dexterity, or brain matter and the face for Composure, for example), which may require a Called Shot at the Storyteller's discretion. The Centimanus can even eat the corpses of the dead to gain the abilities, as long as the body's fresh (typically died within the same Chapter).<br /> <br /> <b>Cost</b>: 3 Pyros<br /> <b>Dice Pool</b>: Resolve + Stamina + Azoth - Attribute Rating (Reflexive), or Resolve + Stamina + Azoth (Instant)<br /> <b>Action</b>: Reflexive, after a successful Bite attack, or Instant, if eating an already dead creature.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:16px\"><b>Roll Results</b></span><br /> <br /> <b>Success</b>: The Freak metabolizes the Ability, adding to their acumen. They gain one dot in the Attribute in question, up to their Trait Maximum, for the rest of the scene. If the victim\u2019s rating in the Attribute is equal to or higher than the Freak\u2019s, they gain two dots. The duration can be increased to 24 hours by spending an additional point of Pyros, and can be extended by spending another Pyros every day, to a maximum of (Azoth) days.<br /> <b>Exceptional Success</b>: The body of the Centimanus processes the meal efficiently, gaining two additional dots in the Attribute instead of one (or thee instead of two), even if this takes them above their trait maximum. This bonus lasts the rest of the scene; any dots above the Freak's Trait Maximum fade, but the remainder last until the end of the chapter.<br /> <b>Failure</b>: The Freak gains nothing.<br /> <b>Dramatic Failure</b>: Something goes wrong when the flesh infuses the body. For the remainder of the scene, the Freak is afflicted with one of the following Tilts: Blinded, Deafened, Insensate, or Poisoned (Moderate). </div> </div> </div>Design Notes<ul><li>I swiped some wording from the Gristlegrinder Kith for Changeling for the Persistent power.</li> <li>There's two uses when this Alembic is charged -- a Reflexive action that can be taken in combat (but often requires a called shot, and a penalty for the rating being stolen), and an Instant action that can be done on a recently dead corpse.</li> <li>I swiped some ideas from Doppelganger -- allowing the expenditure of extra Pyros to extend the duration of the stolen skills and attributes. I wasn't sure I wanted that for the merits, since I currently have them lasting to the end of the Chapter anyway (instead of just the Scene).</li> </ul>I'm curious to know if anyone else had the issues I had with this Alembic, and whether you think my fixes work (or if there's something I missed).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}